@host = http://localhost:5273

### Create
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company": "Contoso",
  "role": "Senior .NET Engineer",
  "jobUrl": "https://contoso.example/jobs/123",
  "notes": "Referred by a friend"
}

### Get the one we just created
GET {{host}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.$.id}}

### List (newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/applications

### Unknown id -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/applications/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Invalid -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company": "    ",
  "role": "",
  "jobUrl": "not-a-url"
}

### Move the created app to Applied (copy the version from the Create response)
PATCH {{host}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Applied", "version": {{create.response.body.$.version}} }

### Illegal move -> 409 (Saved/Applied can't jump to Offer)
PATCH {{host}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Offer", "version": {{create.response.body.$.version}} }

### Bad status string -> 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Hired", "version": 0 }

### Upload a resume
# @name upload
POST {{host}}/api/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BeaconBoundary

--BeaconBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="resume.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# AJ Keiper
Senior .NET engineer. C#, ASP.NET Core, EF Core, PostgreSQL, Azure, Docker.
Led a team building property management software.
--BeaconBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

Resume
--BeaconBoundary--

### Check its status (run a second or two after upload)
GET {{host}}/api/documents/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}

### Wrong file type -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BeaconBoundary

--BeaconBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="resume.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

not really a pdf
--BeaconBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

Resume
--BeaconBoundary--

### Documents for an application (uses the app from your Create request earlier)
GET {{host}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/documents

### Embedding smoke test (dev only, needs Ollama running)
GET {{host}}/dev/embed?text=Senior%20.NET%20engineer%20with%20Kubernetes%20experience

### Ask Beacon (the .http viewer shows it after it finished; use curl.exe to watch it stream)
POST {{host}}/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What cloud and container experience do I have?" }

### Empty question -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": ""}